<title>USA: Immunomedics granted cardiovascular patent.</title>
<headline>Immunomedics granted cardiovascular patent.</headline>
<dateline>MORRIS PLAINS, N.J. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Immunomedics Inc said it won a U.S. Patent covering new methods and agents for the imaging and detection of cardiovascular lesions, such as atherosclerotic plaques, vascular clots, and myocardial infarcts.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company's patent claims involve the use of an antibody conjugate targeted towards identifying the blood cells which contribute to the formation of arterial clots, called monocytes, or to other antigens present at the disease site, such at platelets or fibrin.</p>
<p>Immunomedics was granted U.S. Patent number 5,632,968.</p>
